I don't think it is Bell number, since the Livagian system requires 1--1 co=
rrespondences between members of the two sets, whereas Bell number seems to=
 be the number of possible correspondence patterns among members of a set. =
Each member of each of the two sets may be in correspondence with either ex=
actly one member of the other set or no member of the other set. For reason=
s I won't go into, there are four different sorts of correspondence. So, ea=
ch member of each of the two sets is either in exactly one sort of correspo=
ndence with either exactly one member of the other set or is in no correspo=
ndence with any member of the other set. That must be an easyish formula to=
 find for somebody with more maths nous than me.

And yes, the inflections are compositional.

